e.startswith(\"deepinfer.\"):\n        logger.propagate = True\n    else:\n        logger.propagate = False\n        if _default_handler is not None and _default_handler not in logger.handlers:\n            logger.addHandler(_default_handler)\n    return logger"}], "tool_calls": null, "raw": null, "token_usage": null}], "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_5", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "python_interpreter", "arguments": "write_note(title='stats_logger mechanisms', content='stats_logger.py imports logging via `from deepinfer.logger import init_logger` and creates module logger at line 29: `logger = init_logger(__name__)`. The real queue consumer is `_log_worker(q)`: iterates `for msgs in iter(q.get, None)`, sleeps based on `dist.get_rank() % 8`, then `for m in msgs: logger.info(m)` and sets need_sleep = q.empty(); exceptions go to traceback.print_exc(). Producer `_emit_logs` puts msgs list on queue. The only place to add `extra={\"keep_full_message\": True}` is the `logger.info(m)` call inside _log_worker, preserving queue, ordering, sleep, sentinel and exception handling.', evidence_ids=['ev-ddb5be78a5cf6218d616','ev-c8859274b7c70879ff16','ev-5a3c8c1ca1246b61b813','ev-5abfdabfb975754c6683'], section='')"}}], "error": null, "model_output_message": {"role": "assistant", "content": {"thought": "I have the stats_logger key mechanisms (log worker, emit, logger init). Now write a note for stats_logger, then continue reading the remaining files.", "code": "write_note(title='stats_logger mechanisms', content='stats_logger.py imports logging via `from deepinfer.logger import init_logger` and creates module logger at line 29: `logger = init_logger(__name__)`. The real queue consumer is `_log_worker(q)`: iterates `for msgs in iter(q.get, None)`, sleeps based on `dist.get_rank() % 8`, then `for m in msgs: logger.info(m)` and sets need_sleep = q.empty(); exceptions go to traceback.print_exc(). Producer `_emit_logs` puts msgs list on queue. The only place to add `extra={\"k