me type with prefix f\"{self.name}: {e}\" (TypeError falls back to bare raise); then setattr(owner, self.name, value) caches, so later env changes do not affect value until rearm. Factory staticmethods: int(default=0)->_int, float->_float, bool->_bool, str->_str, str_or_none()->lambda v: v (returns None when unset), int_or_none(), choice(default, choices). New config DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS can follow str_or_none/int_or_none style but must validate >=32 and add a factory (e.g. EnvVar factory method) parsing int and raising ValueError mentioning the name; __get__ prepends the name anyway. `rearm(name)` does setattr(envs, name, _descriptors[name]) so next access re-resolves; `rearm_all()` loops all descriptors doing same. This preserves caching semantics: env edits alone do not change attribute, only rearm+reaccess does.', evidence_ids=['ev-eae82c05a3a3c473d07d','ev-383fc4d6af8a1cd465f1','ev-8d9367024e9cf0226e42'], section='source-note')\nprint(n)"}}], "tool_calls": null, "raw": null, "token_usage": null}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Latest execution feedback:\nExecutor output:\nExecution logs:\n{'note_id': 'source-note', 'sources': ['deepinfer/environ.py', 'deepinfer/logger.py'], 'chars': 1169}\nLast output from code snippet:\nNone\nRecent project tool results:\n[{\"tool\": \"read_range\", \"result\": {\"path\": \"deepinfer/logger.py\", \"file_hash\": \"5b8f8d9947de692353609c1fc2851097d24f9b6ba6004dce1dbfa394dc6d3ec8\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 33, \"evidence_ids\": [\"ev-eae82c05a3a3c473d07d\"], \"delivery\": \"Originals queued for the next model request; large batches may span requests.\"}}, {\"tool\": \"read_range\", \"result\": {\"path\": \"deepinfer/logger.py\", \"file_hash\": \"5b8f8d9947de692353609c1fc2851097d24f9b6ba6004dce1dbfa394dc6d3ec8\", \"start_line\": 33, \"end_line\": 140, \"evidence_ids\": [\"ev-5d7d6c21b53\n[full record remains in run.log]\nae0714d5073c3b4328c8e7cb9\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"ev-ddb5be78a5cf62